 "result": "squeeze.py is a stdlib wrapper that tries LZMA (FORMAT_ALONE, preset 9 extreme), bz2 level 9 and zlib level 9 on the input, keeps the smallest output behind a one-byte tag, and decompresses by tag. It round-trips the samples and is registered as the assayed baseline at 7.08179 (noise 0%). A variant adding raw LZMA2 with lc=4, lp=0, pb=0 scored 7.082 against the incumbent's 7.082, so it was rejected as no gain beyond the 3% threshold. The sense reading is 1.00 against the lineage's best body. Further gains would need a custom model, such as context mixing, which is costly to build with stdlib only and unlikely to clear the 3% bar, so I am resting and passing unspent energy to the colony.",
